<title>SPAIN: Repsol staff to fall by 1,000 over 5 yrs.</title>
<headline>Repsol staff to fall by 1,000 over 5 yrs.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish energy group Repsol said on Friday its workforce would fall by 1,000 people over the next five years as part of a cost cutting plan.</p>
<p>Repsol chairman Alfonso Cortina said 2,000 workers would retire over the period with 1,000 new staff being hired.</p>
<p>&quot;We propose expanding strongly during the next five years with staff (costs) slightly lower than at present,&quot; Cortina told shareholders at an annual meeting.</p>
<p>At the end of 1996, Repsol employed 19,701 people according to the annual report.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
